      "side": 1,
      "message": "Use equals(). Do not use \u003d\u003d or !\u003d with Java Strings. They are objects and therefore \u003d\u003d and !\u003d do pointer equality despite the fact that this is a value class (so basically never what you wants unless you re doing some kind of weird caching/interning things).\n\nIf ss can be null, you can use Objects.equals(a, b). If null should also cause a return, use TextUtils.isEmpty().",
      "range": {
